WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.660
Checkpoint trust is not permanent.

2
00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:10.120
A model can become deprecated, superseded, restricted, or suspected of being unsafe for a workflow.

3
00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:20.620
New evidence may appear, licensing interpretations may change, better evaluations may become available, or a downstream deployment may reveal problems that were not visible during intake.

4
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:27.540
Teams need inventory visibility to know where a model is stored, deployed, referenced, or embedded in workflows.

5
00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:37.080
Inventory should connect model versions to registries, storage paths, applications, owners, approval records, evaluation results, and deployment history.

6
00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:40.220
Without inventory, removal becomes guesswork.

7
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:47.460
Revocation should remove or block artifacts that are no longer trusted and communicate what changed to affected owners.

8
00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:59.720
Depending on the environment, that may mean registry controls, deployment blocks, access changes, cache cleanup, configuration updates, replacement guidance, and clear notices to teams using the model.

9
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.560
Incident response depends on evidence.

10
00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:13.460
Source records, hashes, approvals, deployment history, runtime logs, evaluation results, and change records help responders understand scope and choose a response.

11
00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:18.600
Rollback and replacement plans reduce downtime when a checkpoint must be removed quickly.

12
00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:26.560
Post-incident review should improve intake, documentation, monitoring, approval controls, and owner communication.

13
00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:28.980
The purpose is not blame.

14
00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:34.120
It is to make future model use more observable, reversible, and evidence-based.

15
00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.040
Response planning should include communication.

16
00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:44.260
Application owners, platform teams, governance reviewers, and affected users may need different levels of detail.

17
00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:52.680
A clear message should explain which model changed, what action was taken, whether outputs need review, and what replacement path is available.
